
igrmonty: A monte carlo code for relativistic radiative transport, 
including synchrotron emission and absorption, bremsstrahlung
emission (absorption is negligible), and compton scattering.

This version includes thermal leptons and supports pair enrichment via
`positron_ratio` in parameter files.

For publications, please cite this journal article:
Dolence, J.C., Gammie, C.F., Moscibrodzka, M., and Leung, P.K.: 2009, ApJS 184, 387.
https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2009ApJS..184..387D/abstract
And this repository:
https://github.com/AFD-Illinois/igrmonty

Substantial contributions made by
Ben Ryan
George Wong
Ricardo Castro-Yarza
Chi-kwan Chan

usage: 
  HARM:    grmonty Ns fname M_unit[g] MBH[Msolar] Tp/Te
  bhlight: grmonty Ns fname
  Optional switch: `--run-tests` (or parameter `run_tests 1`) runs internal
  regression tests and exits.

prepped for public release
cfg 18 Apr 2020


## adding new electron distribution functions

1. add new names/parameters to src/model_radiation.h

2. add absorptivity to src/radiation.c:alpha_inv_abs(...)

3. add eDF in src/hotcross.c:dNdgammae_[X], modifying dNdgammae as appropriate

4a. modify eDF functions in src/compton.c
    - dfdgam(...)
    - fdist(...)  -- note overlap with dNdgammae in src/hotcross.c

4b. ensure src/compton.c:sample_beta_distr_num(...) produces reasonable results on edge cases

5a. implement jnu_[X] and int_jnu_[X] in src/jnu_mixed.c. it's likely the integral calls into a table

5b. modify switches in src/jnu_mixed.c  -- jnu(...), jnu_ratio_brems(...), int_jnu(...)


## positron/pair convention

`Ne` from the fluid model is treated as the ion-associated baseline density `n_i`.
When `positron_ratio = f`:
- `n_+ = f * n_i`
- `n_- = (1 + f) * n_i`
- total radiating/scattering leptons `n_lep = (1 + 2 f) * n_i`

GRMONTY applies this internally for synchrotron and scattering.
Bremsstrahlung now includes all thermal pair channels:
- `e-i` scaling `proportional to n_i * n_lep`
- same-sign lepton brems (`e^-e^-` and `e^+e^+`)
- opposite-sign lepton brems (`e^-e^+`)

Downstream scripts should pass baryonic `M_unit` and should not pre-scale
density/M_unit by `(1 + 2 f)`, or pairs will be double-counted.


## wJET controls

Mixed jet modes (`RBETAwJET`, `CRITBETAwJET`) require the following controls
to fully activate the jet/funnel logic:
- `sigma_transition`
- `constant_beta_e0`
- `constant_beta_e0_exponent`
- `jet_sigma_cut`
- `jet_beta_cut`
- `jet_thetae`
- `jet_ne_mult`

`auto_munit_bracket.py` now writes these controls into generated `.par` files
for `wJET` modes. Resolution order is:
1. CLI override (`--sigma-transition`, `--constant-beta-e0`, `--constant-beta-e0-exponent`, `--jet-sigma-cut`, `--jet-beta-cut`, `--jet-thetae`, `--jet-ne-mult`)
2. CSV column if present
3. repo defaults (`2.0`, `0.1`, `0.0`, `10`, `0.1`, `50`, `1`)


## Compton sampling guardrails

The rejection samplers in `src/compton.c` no longer silently halve `Thetae`
after repeated failures. They now fail loudly with `sampling_error` diagnostics
if Klein-Nishina, electron, or beta-distribution sampling exceeds its hard
attempt cap. This is intended to stop invalid production `wJET` runs instead of
quietly mutating the scattering physics.
